// Every RPC requires authenticated x-kokoro-service, x-kokoro-internal-secret,
// x-kokoro-tenant-id, x-kokoro-subject-id, and x-kokoro-request-id transport metadata.
// x-kokoro-scope-kind (personal|project|conversation|skill_package|skill_cover|connector_icon) and
// x-kokoro-scope-id are required. For skill_package, scope-id is the exact
// Platform-owned resource ID; skill_cover and connector_icon use exact owner bindings.
// Storage does not decide Skill authorization; Platform must freshly admit every read.
// Scope is asserted by an authenticated, permitted business owner; body identity is forbidden.
// kokoro-agent has only conversation/artifact-purpose delivery operations;
// web-bff retains ordinary personal/project Asset operations and conversation
// final-Artifact reads, not Artifact writes or package access. kokoro-platform
